2026-09-27T06:52:57.0551144Z     
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0551238Z     The ``pytest`` framework makes it easy to write small tests, yet
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0551358Z     scales to support complex functional testing for applications and libraries.
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0551401Z     
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0551459Z     An example of a simple test:
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0551502Z     
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0551559Z     .. code-block:: python
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0551603Z     
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0551661Z         # content of test_sample.py
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0551710Z         def inc(x):
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0551761Z             return x + 1
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0551803Z     
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0551845Z     
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0551898Z         def test_answer():
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0551951Z             assert inc(3) == 5
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0551994Z     
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0552037Z     
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0552090Z     To execute it::
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0552132Z     
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0552178Z         $ pytest
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0552268Z         ============================= test session starts =============================
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0552318Z         collected 1 items
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0552362Z     
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0552415Z         test_sample.py F
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0552457Z     
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0552536Z         ================================== FAILURES ===================================
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0552634Z         _________________________________ test_answer _________________________________
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0552678Z     
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0552729Z             def test_answer():
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0552784Z         >       assert inc(3) == 5
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0552836Z         E       assert 4 == 5
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0552889Z         E        +  where 4 = inc(3)
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0552932Z     
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0552993Z         test_sample.py:5: AssertionError
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0553082Z         ========================== 1 failed in 0.04 seconds ===========================
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0553126Z     
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0553170Z     
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0553557Z     Thanks to ``pytest``'s detailed assertion introspection, you can simply use plain ``assert`` statements. See `getting-started <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/getting-started.html#our-first-test-run>`_ for more examples.
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0553600Z     
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0553644Z     
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0553758Z     Features
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0553808Z     --------
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0553850Z     
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0554094Z     - Detailed info on failing `assert statements <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/assert.html>`_ (no need to remember ``self.assert*`` names)
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0554142Z     
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0554193Z     - `Auto-discovery
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0554347Z       <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/explanation/goodpractices.html#python-test-discovery>`_
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0554463Z       of test modules and functions
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0554508Z     
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0554645Z     - `Modular fixtures <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/explanation/fixtures.html>`_ for
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0554737Z       managing small or parametrized long-lived test resources
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0554782Z     
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0554919Z     - Can run `unittest <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/unittest.html>`_ (or trial)
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0554977Z       test suites out of the box
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0555026Z     
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0555083Z     - Python 3.10+ or PyPy3
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0555125Z     
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0555367Z     - Rich plugin architecture, with over 1300+ `external plugins <https://docs.pytest.org/en/latest/reference/plugin_list.html>`_ and thriving community
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0555413Z     
2026-09-27T06:52:57.0555455Z     
